                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/4352: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Brazil</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Gordon</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-11-21T17:00:00-05:00">November 21, 1934—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>173. Your 321, November 19, 6 p.m. In view of the reply recently addressed by
                    this Government to the Secretary General of the League of Nations, it does not
                    seem probable that the action proposed by the Minister for Foreign Affairs will
                    create the impression in Geneva that the Brazilian Government is attempting to
                    speak for the United States. Should any misunderstanding in Geneva result,
                    however, the Department will take the steps necessary to make clear that the
                    Brazilian initiative was taken without prior consultation with the United States
                    and that the position of this Government remains that manifested in the last
                    communication addressed to the Secretary General of the League. It is desirable
                    that you do not discuss this question at this moment with the Minister for
                    Foreign Affairs.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
